   "Characteristic curves: x axis is absolute log exposure in lux-seconds (exposure: daylight 1/100 s), as printed with bar notation (2.0 with an overbar = -2.0); the axis runs -2.0 to 2.0 and the curves are drawn from about -2.0 to about 1.61. The sheet prints no Log H Ref, so log_h_ref is null.",
   "Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/50 s, density 0.2 above D-min, Status M, process C-41; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in ergs/cm2) as printed, and on this sheet the axis runs -2.0 to 2.0 (the plotted curves lie between about 0.0 and 1.7). The yellow-forming (b) curve spans about 410 to 490 nm, the magenta-forming (g) about 490 to 590 nm and the cyan-forming (r) about 570 to 670 nm, so the three curves are drawn only over their own band and not over the whole spectrum.",
   "Spectral-dye-density plot has only 'Midscale Neutral' (mid) and 'Minimum Density' (min), no separate c/m/y dyes; both are solid lines. Both start at 400 nm already high (mid about 2.3, min about 1.7) and fall steeply.",
   "Printed checks (Status M red-filter densities of a normally exposed negative): grey card 0.75 to 0.95; lightest paper-gray-scale step 1.10 to 1.30.",
